+PC2 VERDICT: ACCEPT-WITH-CHANGES — blocking revisions required before implementation. Read-only review of docs/plan/scale_stage46/plan_v3.md against HEAD 7bcb07a4571ca242416f90b31644a9c4801fa7ba; no files created, edited, deleted, or committed.
+
+BLOCKING FINDINGS
+
+B1 — Streaming the stage-4 writer does not bound the stage-4/5 pipeline.
+Plan: plan_v3.md:92-99,132-136,171-177. Evidence: roi_export.py:208-211 shares coverage before serialization, but candidates.py:239-254 immediately read_text/json.loads the complete export and retain every parsed coverage copy; both sides remain alive through :470-547. candidates.py:96-97 also hashes entire exports with read_bytes. Stage 5 keeps all four exports via confirm_pairs.py:65-72,125-132. Dropping maps or using iterencode does not remove these allocations. Additionally, electrode_map.py:502 deep-copies all layer coverage per region, so even the pre-serialization map is O(R*N) metadata, not just packed masks and links.
+Read-only repro using actual compute_electrode_maps/export_review_rois with mocked filesystem sinks: one region, N=100 linked cases -> 3,911,512 JSON bytes, 8,066,788 B retained after parse; N=200 -> 14,962,012 bytes, 30,671,960 B retained. Parsed row coverages are distinct objects. These tiny-frame cases already demonstrate approximately quadratic scaling; 1,682 cases is about 1 GB export / 2 GB parsed objects PER SIDE on the same identity lengths, before real datasets, hashes, read buffers, and additional regions. This contradicts the <=3 GB stage-4 and <=2 GB stage-5 targets.
+Required: assign a concrete byte-preserving bounded export/consumer design (avoid reparse in candidates, preserve sharing or project fields without materializing duplicated coverage, stream hashes; give stage-5 readers their own bounded parser/projection or explicit pre-read rejection). If retaining eager consumers, define and test a fail-fast size/structure limit BEFORE read_text/read_bytes/json.loads, include all live sides and region coverage, and say which real-scale cases will be refused. Q2 cannot remain the sole disposition, and T2/T5 must own confirm_pairs changes or a deliberate refusal gate; a schema change is not inherently necessary.
+
+B2 — The proposed publish-on-success sequence loses the old set on publication failure.
+Plan: :123-126,140-142. It deletes old local_delta*/window_sensitivity* and then renames new files; ENOSPC/OSError/Ctrl-C after the first deletion cannot leave old outputs intact. A staging directory inside out is not an atomic directory swap, and documenting a non-atomic window does not supply rollback/restart recovery.
+Evidence: pipeline.py:978-980 currently calls the numeric and HTML writers separately. T4 does not own pipeline.py, so it has no stated transaction owner spanning both calls and all JSON/CSV/HTML/thumb metadata/PNG outputs. The Phase A RA2/RA3/RA4 publication lessons apply directly.
+Required: explicit full-set transaction ownership and file allowlist, a preserved old generation/backups, durable commit decision, rollback/roll-forward and fail-closed recovery when state cannot be read. Add pipeline.py to T4 or define an equally concrete coordinated writer API. Test faults before/after every delete/replace/commit/cleanup/read boundary, plus restart and pre-existing unrelated files/PNGs. Before commit failure preserves OLD; after a durable commit recovery preserves NEW. Do not promise OLD on every possible failure.
+
+B3 — Stage-6 admission is missing costs and has no feasible call contract in the task scope.
+Plan: :104-114,137-142 prices layouts + rows + writer transient, but must also price the new 256-entry unpack cache, <=64 full named-case records, pinned overview masks, simultaneous decode/eviction temporaries, row/reason strings, sensitivity/ranking/explained structures and retained datasets/AreaResults, using the largest appropriate shapes from BOTH models. At 1500² the two explicitly proposed mask caches alone can retain 576,000,000 + 144,000,000 B. An 8-case layout cache needs an explicit per-side/per-case/two-layout multiplier; overview_layouts can pin another two masks per (side, frame) (local_delta_report.py:334-337). A measured average ~10 KB/row is not an upper bound on variable reasons/provenance.
+The CLI guard runs BEFORE correspondence loading/binding at pipeline.py:967-969 and presently accepts neither P nor sizes; the library guard is local_delta.py:375-377 and the HTML guard is local_delta_report.py:284-286. Pipeline is outside T3 scope. A row-aware check only in the writer is too late.
+Required: specify phase-wise peak formulas (max of compute vs row/report phases, not arbitrary addition), guard inputs and all call sites, count actual ready/blocked pairs and validated sizes before compute/allocation, and add pipeline.py to T3. Charge/guard link/coverage growth in T2 before allocation as well. Tests must assert measured peak <= priced budget AND zero expensive calls before a one-byte-below refusal, on 3.8 and 3.11, with asymmetric frames, many groups/regions/links, oversized P/sizes and cache eviction. --compact-json is not a remedy for retained result.rows or HTML; it currently only removes JSON rows after computing them (local_delta.py:734-740), and after streaming it may barely change peak RAM.
+
+B4 — The proposed benchmark can measure blocked/no-op work and misses two optimized stage-6 paths.
+Plan: :148-158 says today's generator plus layouts/assignments/matches. Today's generator writes constant CSV area 0.01 for every nontrivial mask (benchmark_scale_compare.py:50-54), and write_config omits roles (98-103). CSV mismatch is retained at real_hotspot.py:978-984; measure_full_mask then makes map coverage partial (electrode_map.py:432-449), ROI export blocks it (roi_export.py:190-191), and the real role gate separately blocks missing roles (candidates.py:139-153). confirm_pairs.py:198-201 refuses such query rows. I reproduced both the map_coverage_incomplete and missing-role blocking in memory.
+More importantly, confirm_pairs.py:306-309,325-330 deliberately leaves the candidate side endpoints=None and repeats_per_frame=None. Thus the generated stage-5 correspondences NEVER exercise named-case loading (local_delta.py:401-404 needs endpoints on BOTH sides), and explained_fraction returns early (594-598).
+Required: consistent CSV areas, explicit role policy, complete inventory and assets, and asserted ready ROI/query/confirmed-pair counts; assert exact P*|sizes|*32 output rows and that named-pair, jitter and explained-union branches actually ran. Keep an end-to-end stage-5-produced fixture, plus separately labelled correspondence fixtures with both endpoint bindings and repeats to benchmark the full T3 contract without changing stage-5 output semantics. Explicitly run centered/high-link-volume AND many-separated-component profiles, distinct/shared electrode pairs, equal/asymmetric frame sizes, overlapping/disjoint windows, multiple P points including a guard-refusal boundary. Distinct electrode layout rectangles alone do not create electrode-map components: stage 4 uses hotspot masks. Merely accepting exit code 3 is not successful scale validation.
+
+B5 — Asset memoization/lazy loading needs a validation-preserving contract.
+Plan: :93 and :110-111. A process-wide (path, sha256) memo is underspecified: the same relative path occurs in different roots, value_semantics changes the decoded mask (numeric_images.py:47-74), and _asset checks frame shape and valid equality per use (roi_export.py:45-55). check_asset_manifest also binds identity/endpoints/failure type/source hash separately (:74-123). Caching fully decoded arrays for every distinct path would recreate the memory problem; caching only a successful validation without re-authenticating current bytes would miss a file changed between exports.
+_Assets currently validates the complete manifest and then loads in dataset order under one try; a second-read failure preserves earlier masks but suppresses all later masks and records a global reason (local_delta_report.py:151-171). Per-case lazy exceptions can therefore change HTML/thumb notes and which later layouts are available. This may be a desirable semantic change, but it is not proven byte-equivalent by 'same arrays, same _render'.
+Required: invocation-scoped, bounded metadata memo with absolute root-resolved file identity and relevant decoding semantics; preserve current hash/integrity checks and per-binding shape/valid checks. Specify failure-order behavior for _Assets or explicitly obtain acceptance for any narrowed equivalence contract. Oracle cases must include same paths in different roots, same bytes/opposite semantics, different valid masks/frame shapes, missing/invalid assets and mutation/failure between validation and use. Scope the unpack cache to the owning AreaResults/invocation, or keep owner identity alive; a persistent cache keyed only by id(group) risks stale hits on ID reuse.
+
+B6 — Loader/corruption claims and I/O acceptance contradict the actual command path.
+Plan: :12-17,21-23,39-42,49-50,78-80,135-136. pipeline._real_source ALWAYS calls load_real_manifest (pipeline.py:11-29); that function hashes and DECODES every observed mask and validates dtype/shape/area (real_hotspot.py:507-521). Stage 3 invokes it at electrode_png.py:252-262; stages 4, 5 and 6 invoke it twice per side via source-kind probes and subsequent dataset setup (candidates.py:418,176/183; confirm_pairs.py:439,447; pipeline.py:961,964-965 with :942-950).
+Consequences: stage 5 is not 'no mask access/otherwise seconds'; header-only map validation does NOT stop the normal CLI detecting a corrupt nonrepresentative NPZ, since it was checked in this run, not merely at stage-1 import; and SIMCOMPARE_IO_COUNTERS cannot show only one mask decode per case across the whole candidates command. Correct expectation is the retained authentication passes plus one representative load, with a separate map-only counter. Do not remove authentication as an incidental way to satisfy T2.
+Also T5_benchmark.md:103-107 explicitly reports 586.6 s for a compare of BOTH models, so compute_areas(reference)+compute_areas(target) is not two such 587 s compares; stage-6 time must separate load validation, both-model compute, windows, report. Stage-3 ~0.15 GB is a decode-buffer subtotal, not RSS: _dataset_bytes explicitly omits strings/dicts (electrode_png.py:280-284) while configured_dataset holds multiple metadata copies (real_hotspot.py:1003-1009,1051-1054).
+Required: correct the per-command cost/I/O model and corruption/error-precedence tests before accepting the implementation contract; keep shared load/compare admission/provenance unchanged unless separately justified and regression-tested.
+
+ADVISORIES / ADDITIONAL ACCEPTANCE DETAILS
+
+A1 — The central math changes are sound with qualifications. OR all eligible cases per distinct electrode before int64 count addition; duplicate/shared endpoints must not count twice. Derive sorted region electrode names from the exact same eligible observed links; inside is contained in valid, so original_mask & inside equals active & inside. Preserve case sorting, record reasons/status/source_ca/tolerances and full original masks when reconstructing MaskRecords; outside_valid alone is not all record metadata. Drop original full-mask MaskRecord references after packing, otherwise observed still retains the N full arrays. Keep full-frame gather order and one area cache per region. I ran 40 seeded complete-map comparisons on Python 3.8.20/numpy 1.21.6 with shared electrodes, invalid cells, fractional pitch/origin: the actual measure_union with per-region cache equalled the current complete output exactly, and names-from-links equalled region.electrodes.
+
+A2 — Oracle independence must be enforceable. Rewriting imports and then demanding the files hash-match git show verbatim (:64-65,130) are inconsistent; freeze source bytes plus a separate loader/import rewiring, or normalize only an audited import delta and hash against a checked-in base digest (works without git). Frozen candidates dynamically calls production pipeline helpers (candidates.py:170-183,220-232; pipeline.py:886-888 imports production map/export), so explicitly route the entire oracle call graph to the frozen implementations. Include validation/missing-assets/SourceCA-conservation cases, both compact/full writers, empty/all-blocked tables, non-ASCII/reasons, equivalent-but-distinct frames, non-byte-aligned widths and multi-layer/group eviction. Same-result writer equality alone cannot validate T3; retain result/metadata equality plus end-to-end candidate tree equality. Add a deliberate production perturbation test proving the oracle catches it.
+
+A3 — JSON/CSV streaming is feasible, but use a real list-compatible adapter/custom encoder and bypass whole-result to_dict/json_value. A plain object with only __len__/__iter__ raises TypeError in JSONEncoder.iterencode; an in-memory list subclass with those overrides matched dumps byte-for-byte. report.json_value recursively materializes lists (report.py:20-30), and LocalDeltaResult.to_dict already traverses rows (:335-344). Preserve key order, trailing newlines, UTF-8 behavior, null/boolean/container CSV rendering and each table's actual first-seen key order; add empty result/one-size/rank-agreement cases on both Python versions. No need to modify the shared report.json_value and risk stage 2.
+
+A4 — Report scope and numerical estimates need precise wording. Existing ETX JOBS intentionally exclude integrated report (build_etx_stage_runners.py:70-75; configs/etx/README.md:23); final_report.py:18-19 requires the older numeric comparison schema and :381-387 eagerly parses stage-6 JSON/CSVs. Keeping that existing exclusion is reasonable if the coordinator explicitly states 'report' here means local_delta.html; do not describe the broader Phase B brief as including scalable integrated report. Stage-6 current guard layout charge is 34,424,780,832 B for BOTH 1,682-case/1262² models, not 17.2 GB; actual retained cropped layouts are 10,715,308,832 B for both models. At 1500² those become 42,050,000,000 and 15,138,000,000 B. The direction of the proposed correction is right. Remaining CPU terms include O(R^2) candidate merging (candidates.py:77-88), O(P^2) explained-window overlap grouping (local_delta.py:577-580), and the requested-area _slabs reduction that measure_union still repeats before using area_cache (measurement.py:116-141); measure these with many components/overlaps instead of attributing all time to unpack.
+
+A5 — Stage-1/2 ETX compatibility is achievable but requires explicit regression evidence. Restrict pipeline edits needed by B2/B3 to stage-6 orchestration; keep load_real_manifest, configured_dataset defaults, estimate_area_bytes, assignment hashes and resource_estimate provenance stable. Re-run old sealed NPZ and legacy NPY imports through stage 2; compare stage-1/2 outputs under identical runtime/config/path/provenance, and verify every rebuilt embedded source/hash (including the general bundle if it is distributed). Config comments may change cfg hashes, so the N=50 byte diff requires identical config bytes/canonical paths and fixed producer/timestamp fields, not merely two different temporary directories. Read-only sharing of raw/metadata and packed-region internals must not leak a new dataclass field through ElectrodeMaps.to_dict (electrode_map.py:285-295) or change the public mask field/value.
+
+VALIDATION / LIMITS
+- Read repository and prior RA2/RA3/RA4 evidence, no external research needed.
+- Actual in-memory export/parse scaling, benchmark blocking probes, estimator arithmetic, and JSON encoder adapter probes ran on .venv Python 3.11; 40 exact map/cache/derived-name equivalence probes ran on Python 3.8.20/numpy 1.21.6.
+- Python probes disabled bytecode and installed an audit hook denying filesystem mutations (virtual output sinks were mocked). Initial 3.8 hook also blocked opening /dev/null; corrected that device-only restriction and reran successfully.
+- No implementation candidate exists yet; no claim of full-suite, filesystem recovery, or real-scale benchmark execution.
+- git diff --check passes; HEAD unchanged; git status retains only the pre-existing untracked docs/plan/scale_stage46/ directory. Report delivered through Orca, no report file.
\ No newline at end of file
